lisa-design:
- The preset is inlined into the generated global config (cmd/renovate-config config) instead of `extends: github>compliance-framework/workflows//renovate/default`: the run uses the preset at the ref it runs from, and needs no read of this repo with a token scoped to other repos. Repos' own renovate.json still merges on top.
- Repo list = every repo in the manifest (not only release: true), optional `repos` subset; empty selection fails before minting a token (an unscoped token would reach every org repo).
- OPA is disabled everywhere except api/mock-api (a superset of "agent and policy repos": plugins also follow api via ccf-bump); in api it is its own `renovate/opa` group, automerge false.
- Internal packages off also covers `compliance-framework/**` (actions and reusable workflows such as this repo), since ccf-bump owns the `@v1` refs; spec named only the github.com/ and ghcr.io/ prefixes.
- ccf-release-bot lacks Commit statuses; the generated config sets statusCheckWhen.minimumReleaseAge "never" (internalChecksFilter strict makes the status redundant). Reads of statuses work because all repos are public.
- Dry runs mint a read-only token (no workflows permission); live runs get contents/PRs/issues/workflows write. dry_run and manifest fallbacks in job env cover scheduled runs (no inputs).
- Grouped PR commit type: Renovate picks the highest type among a group's upgrades (fix > chore), so a group with any runtime dep is fix(deps). Runtime = require/dependencies + Dockerfile final stage + Go toolchain directive.
- Renovate pinned to 44.145.1 via renovate-version (action default is the floating '44').

